---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { meta } from '../lib/data';
const wallets = Object.entries(meta.wallets);
---

<Layout title="About — Proof of a Person">
  <article class="text-page">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Proof of Attendance Protocol, 2019 to 2026. POAP began as about a hundred
      badges for hackathon attendees at ETHDenver in February 2019, became a
      company, minted some 7.6 million tokens for about 46,000 issuers, entered
      maintenance mode on 2026-03-16, created its last drop on 2026-07-31 and
      announced its wind-down on 2026-08-03. The tokens stay on-chain.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site reads the four letters its own way. A collection of POAPs is
      proof of a person: where they went, what they cared about, who they stood
      next to. Jamie always said POAP was about people and not money, unlike so
      much of crypto. In his words from 2023, "POAPs are meant to collect and
      curate memories, not make money."
    </p>
    <h2>The data</h2>
    <p>
      Everything here comes from{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/jthingelstad/poap-archive">
        jthingelstad/poap-archive
      </a>
      , a capture made on {meta.captured} from the POAP Compass API, the Gnosis
      chain, POAP's asset host, thingelstad.com and the community snapshot at
      poaparchive.com. Addresses and ENS names are public on-chain and are shown
      as POAP showed them: the primary ENS name where one is set, the shortened
      address otherwise.
    </p>
    <h2>Jamie's wallets</h2>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <th>ENS</th>
        <th>Address</th>
      </tr>
      {wallets.map(([address, name]) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{name}</td>
          <td>
            <code>{address}</code>
          </td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </table>
    <h2>Artwork</h2>
    <p>
      Drop artwork is served from a copy taken from assets.poap.xyz while it was
      still up.
    </p>
    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Built with Astro from a JSON export of the archive, hosted on S3 and
      CloudFront, with Tinylytics for private visit counts and kudos. The site
      repository is{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/jthingelstad/poap.thingelstad.xyz">
        jthingelstad/poap.thingelstad.xyz
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
